pref-title = Confucius
pref-help = Native research agent for Zotero.
pref-model-title = Model
pref-model-help = These fields are the active endpoint. Add and switch additional endpoints in the Confucius workspace (⚙ Settings).
pref-base-url = Base URL
pref-api-key = API key
pref-model = Model
pref-max-tokens = Max tokens (0 = provider default)
pref-bridge-title = Local API
pref-bridge-help = Bearer token for the local MCP and HTTP API. Requests only succeed on 127.0.0.1 with this token.
pref-mcp-json = Extra MCP servers JSON (optional)
pref-agent-title = Agent behavior
pref-agent-help = Streaming and turn limits apply to every native model endpoint.
pref-stream-responses = Stream model output live
pref-max-iterations = Max model rounds (all endpoints)
pref-max-tool-calls = Max tool calls (all endpoints)
pref-memory-location = Memories live in < Zotero data >/confucius/memory/ as one markdown file each.
pref-runtime-title = Agent Runtimes
pref-runtime-help = Codex and Kimi connect through the local sidecar and use their official CLI login state. Desktop login tokens are never copied.
pref-runtime-refresh = Check Runtime status
pref-runtime-kimi-path = Kimi executable (optional override)
pref-runtime-kimi-save = Save Kimi path
pref-runtime-sidecar-connected = Sidecar connected
pref-runtime-sidecar-offline = Sidecar offline — run npm run sidecar in the Confucius repository.
pref-runtime-ready = ready
pref-runtime-unavailable = unavailable
pref-runtime-auth-required = sign-in required
pref-runtime-error = error
pref-memory-title = Research memory
pref-memory-help = New installs and upgrades default to review. Manual additions, edits, and deletions are always proposed for review.
pref-memory-consent = After each completed turn
pref-memory-off = Off — do not extract
pref-memory-review = Review — save editable proposals
pref-memory-auto = Auto — save without a proposal
pref-security-title = Safety capabilities
pref-security-help = Every task starts Zotero-only: no Shell and no arbitrary file writes. Zotero writes always show a before/after review.
pref-security-workspace = Workspace access can be enabled only for an individual task after choosing and confirming an absolute directory. Commands and file modifications still require one-time or task-level approval.
